Subject: Run initdb's helper commands without /bin/sh
Purpose: initdb starts the bootstrap and single-user server with popen() and system() commands containing quotes and redirections, and find_other_exec() probes versions with popen(). A FROM scratch image has no shell, so with PG_NO_SHELL defined these calls go through a small interpreter (words, quotes, backslash, < > 2> 2>&1) built on posix_spawn; shell syntax it does not implement (pipes, &, ;, $, backquotes, globs) is refused with EINVAL instead of being run wrongly. Without PG_NO_SHELL the code is upstream's.
Components: src/common/noshell.c (new), src/include/common/noshell.h (new), src/common/exec.c, src/bin/initdb/initdb.c, src/common/Makefile
Checks: tests/native/noshell-test.c (quotes, redirections, 2>&1, pipes for r and w, exit status, refused syntax) and ./dcb musl make native-test, which runs initdb in a container that has no /bin/sh
Origin: own
Ported-from: 18.6 (native/0002-no-shell-spawn.patch) for 16.15 by scripts/port-patches.js
Ported-from: 16.15 (native/pg16/0002-no-shell-spawn.patch) for 15.19 by scripts/port-patches.js

